    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #280\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-197-mail-live-sync-03-06-add-gmail-pub-sub-thr_7eyu3b7p4s`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis implements issue #197 (Gmail Pub/Sub history synchronization), the Gmail-mode analogue of #196's bounded IMAP IDLE lifecycle:\n\n- **`gmailWatchLifecycle.ts`** — `createGmailWatchLifecycleFactory` hosts two long-lived loops per account: a renewal loop that registers/renews `users.watch` daily and persists both the expiry and (on first registration only) the history cursor, and a pull loop that consumes Cloud Pub/Sub notifications, validates them against the account's own email, and hands matches off to the existing idempotent `enqueueMailAccountSync` job — acknowledging only after that durably commits.\n- **`gmailPubSubClient.ts`** — the real transport over Gmail's REST `users.watch` and Cloud Pub/Sub's REST pull/acknowledge endpoints, with a bounded response reader, explicit field validation instead of unchecked type casts, and per-notification error isolation so one malformed message can't block an entire pull batch.\n- **`mailAccountSyncStateStore.ts`** — `recordGmailWatchRegistration` persists the watch expiry unconditionally and seeds the history cursor via `COALESCE` only when none exists yet, satisfying the \"persist history/expiry\" requirement without letting a later renewal regress a cursor the reconcile pass has since advanced.\n- **`gmailWatchLifecycle.test.ts`** — 9 tests covering registration/persistence (including the cursor-seeding and non-regression cases), notification handling and jobKey dedup, account-validation filtering, duplicate/redelivery safety, pull-error backoff, renewal cadence, and stop() semantics.\n\nThis round of commits also addresses all 4 findings from the automated code review on PR #280: removed dead test code, capped the Pub/Sub/Gmail response body size, replaced unchecked type casts with explicit field validation, isolated malformed-notification parsing so it can't fail an entire pull batch, and fixed the previously unmet acceptance criterion around persisting the `users.watch` historyId.\n\nType-check is clean. The full backend suite passes except for intermittent `out of shared memory` Postgres errors in the embedded test cluster under full-suite concurrency, which hit a different, non-overlapping set of unrelated pre-existing files each run and pass cleanly (116/116) when re-run together with this issue's own tests in isolation — confirmed as environment resource contention, not a regression from this change.",
